{"name":"Nightingale Grey","hex":"#baaea3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nightingale","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Eurasian and African songbird, Luscinia megarhynchos, family Muscicapidae, famed for its beautiful singing at night; a common nightingale."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of flannel scarf with sleeves, formerly worn by invalids when sitting up in bed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightingale"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Common nightingale","blocks":[{"text":"The common nightingale, rufous nightingale or simply nightingale, is a small passerine bird which is known for its powerful and beautiful song, often described as one of the most beautiful sounds in nature. An Old World flycatcher, it belongs to a group of more terrestrial species, often called chats. Its range partly overlaps with that of the more northerly thrush nightingale, a closely related species with which hybrids have occurred."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_Common_nightingale_-_Nachtegaal_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_Common_nightingale_-_Nachtegaal_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_nightingale","wikidata":"Q25393"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswe